WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.750
Christmas Party
Come all! On 12/24 we will be
holding a Christmas Party!
Location: Warehouse: Block 3
Time: 8:00 PM

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:29.750
Epimetheus...

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.410
Do it.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:45.910
What's going on?

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:17.500
Kono sora no shita itsu made mo

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:21.910
Sagashi tsuzuketa yume

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:23.500
Hitorikiri...

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.120
Doko e minna tabidatsu no?

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.660
Kioku no hibi ga toozakaru

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:39.410
Ano koro no egao wa

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:46.160
Mune no naka ima wo sasaeteta

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:56.500
Mugon no yokogao de anata mo watashi mo kitto

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.040
Kizu yue no persona wakatte ita yo

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:02.620
Kizu yue no persona wakatte ita yo

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:07.290
Shiawase no tame ni ai no tame dakara to

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:11.750
Zankoku na tatakai wo kuri kaeshite

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:15.370
Sore de mo namida ga tomaranai

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:19.790
Negau kokoro wa issho

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:26.540
Sorezore no mirai ga yobunda

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:33.450
Night

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:35.700
Th-this... is too cruel!

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:38.950
Has Tsukimijima been destroyed?

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.790
Are there any survivors?

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:41.830
Still unknown!

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:44.580
Naze!

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.500
What the hell?! I heard that
Tsukimijima is under attack.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:51.620
Ma'am!

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:54.700
Right. We are currently working
to rescue them.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.000
How's Ami?

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.750
She's okay, at least for now.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:00.790
For now...?

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:04.660
We just received a warning from Turiavita.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.250
It said they have captured Ami.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.250
Ami...?

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:13.200
Miss Naze.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:14.200
Right.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.410
"We will return Ami Futami
at the designated location

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.250
"in exchange for Imber and Nebula."

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.000
"If this condition is not met,

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.370
"Ami's survival will not be guaranteed."

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.870
Their methods are twisted.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:31.370
If they want our iDOLs, they should
come at us head first, fair and square!

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:36.330
It seems that Turiavita had their sights
set on Miss Futami when they attacked.

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:40.160
They probably intended to take her
hostage from the beginning.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.290
We're heading out, Idiot Ribbon!

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.290
Could you hold off on that for a bit?

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.580
Nubilum...

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:22.080
It would be most troublesome
if you acted rashly with this.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:26.370
Of course, we can't give in
to Turiavita's demands either.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:28.040
As such, we must carefully handle-

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.450
"Rashly"?! You call rescuing a friend
who has been captured "acting rashly"?!

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:35.040
Depending on the time and situation.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:36.200
That's horrible!

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:42.160
You see, the enemy is hoping that
we will behave just as Iori is right now.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:46.500
We can't simply walk into something
that is obviously a trap, now can we?

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.370
The Geneva Headquarters are
already taking action.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:55.370
Until we receive orders from Headquarters,
we are to continue to stay on standby.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:01.500
But there's no way we'll just
abandon Ami to her fate, right?

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.750
Chihaya... Kisaragi.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:22.950
You will be our bait.
The bait needed to lure out Imber.

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.790
Bait...?

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:38.870
Just for that, you...
did something so terrible?!

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.620
If it would help me get Imber back,
I'd do anything!

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:46.160
You're still going on about that?!

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:51.500
Imber makes the most beautiful sounds
when he's together with Haruka!

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.830
It's a sound he never made with you!

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:55.540
Does that still hold true?

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.040
Can you say with full confidence

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.790
that Haruka Amami and Imber
are closely linked?

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:04.790
But even so-!

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.200
You sure run off at the mouth.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:27.330
Imber belongs to me.
I won't let anyone have him.

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:29.250
Don't you think that's enough?

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:49.200
Makoto...?

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:54.330
Well, I'd hate to lose Ami Futami's talents...

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:57.830
But I would not call her
an indispensable asset.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.790
She is nothing more than
a consumable product.

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:03.450
Have you made your move?

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:06.580
I arranged for them to send out the MSA.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:10.580
11:05 Mondenkind OA Naval Base

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.160
Any minute now, their unit will set out.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:12.580
So you're dispatching an assault unit?

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:13.580
Same Time, Mondenkind EA
Aerobatics Training Grounds

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.080
Do you plan on starting a war?

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:17.580
I was under the impression that

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:20.620
the war has been going on
ever since that day 16 years ago.

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:22.790
Rubbish.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:24.330
My apologies then.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:26.580
Actually, on top of my rude statement,

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.830
I would like to offer
my opinion on something.

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.120
Let us hear it.

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:34.700
What would you think
of prepping Vulturius?

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:36.540
Vulturius?

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:39.370
It would be for the worst-case scenario.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:42.790
The saying goes, "Take Fortune
by the forelock," you know?

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.120
Very well. We shall take
it into consideration.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:52.540
I appreciate it.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:55.790
It's me.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:08:01.830
I am terribly sorry. As of yet, we are
still unable to track Yukiho Hagiwara's trail.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:04.120
But we found evidence of her leaking
Ami Futami's schedule to an outside source

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:07.910
through the computer terminal
that she left in her dorm room.

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:11.790
We believe she guided them
in the assault on Tsukimijima.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:17.290
Just as I suspected. Very well.
Please continue your investigation.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:19.910
My, my.

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:25.450
So her access to the mainframe was
camouflage to divert our attention, huh?

00:08:25.450 --> 00:08:28.950
Very well, but I won't let you
continue to have your way.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.160
What is it, Suzushiro?

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:38.450
Oh, well, I just saw Yukiho.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.540
Huh? She isn't there.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:43.040
What's keeping you?
We're heading out, you two!

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:44.580
Right!

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.250
Suzushiro!

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:47.370
Coming!

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.160
Ma'am!

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:02.410
I'm begging you, Ma'am.
Please let us go rescue Ami.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.410
You girls...

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:08.580
I can't wait for orders from HQ!

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.830
I know how you feel,

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:14.500
but we are here to protect the world
from the threat presented by Drops.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:18.660
That is why we are permitted
to have the iDOLs and you Masters.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:23.660
As members of Mondenkind,
you should be well aware of that!

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:27.950
As such, we can't simply use the iDOLs
for things outside of missions.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:29.200
This isn't right.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:50.660
Even if it's for the sake of our iDOLs,
it just isn't right to leave Ami to her fate!

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:55.830
I mean, aren't both Ami
and the iDOLs our friends?!

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:59.410
But to save one we have
to sacrifice the other...

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:00.700
Idiot Ribbon...

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.540
We don't know that for sure.

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.370
Then-

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:08.790
At any rate, I don't have any more time
to waste on arguing with you.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.790
Aren't all three of you currently
on special standby?

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.580
You should go back.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:16.250
Ma'am!

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:17.330
Ritsuko!

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:18.250
Forehead!
Ritsuko!

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.660
We're leaving, Idiot Ribbon.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:36.250
No matter what they think,
this is our only choice.

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:40.830
We no longer have...
the option to turn back.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.660
Isn't the same true for you as well?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.120
I'm fully aware that our mission
is to fight off Drops.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:55.500
But that doesn't mean we're tools
that they can use and then throw away!

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.580
Don't you feel the same way?

00:10:59.160 --> 00:11:02.000
Ami must feel so alone.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.000
Haruka!

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:09.910
Yukiho!

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:16.290
Attention everyone.

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:18.660
In 20 minutes, we will execute
the revised electric field.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:20.040
Hey, how do you think this
is going to turn out?
In 20 minutes, we will execute
the revised electric field.

00:11:20.040 --> 00:11:21.160
Hey, how do you think this
is going to turn out?
We will issue a warning three minutes in advance.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:22.580
This is no time to be doing this...
We will issue a warning three minutes in advance.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:24.250
This is no time to be doing this...
Chief, I am sending you
the Tragheit Module's status.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.870
We're doing it precisely
because of the situation!
Chief, I am sending you
the Tragheit Module's status.

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:25.950
We're doing it precisely
because of the situation!
Line 1: Blue. Line 2: Green. Line 7: Yellow.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.160
Line 1: Blue. Line 2: Green. Line 7: Yellow.

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:30.250
We've just gotta focus on
doin' what we can.
Line 1: Blue. Line 2: Green. Line 7: Yellow.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.450
That goes for everyone!

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.250
Right!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:38.700
I'm going to crack into the system
for a minute and draw everyone's attention.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:40.540
The two of you can take that chance to go.

00:11:40.540 --> 00:11:41.830
Draw their attention how?

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:43.950
For you, that's a pretty good idea.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:47.120
After all, negotiating with our superiors
won't get us anywhere.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:51.160
But... is it okay? Really?

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:55.410
What?! Why the hesitation now?
Don't you want to save Ami?

00:11:55.410 --> 00:11:56.450
I want to save her!

00:11:57.830 --> 00:11:59.160
I want to save her, but...

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:03.200
It's true that this will
inconvenience everyone here.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:06.370
Then what should we do?! At this rate...!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:10.330
Right. At this rate, Ami will...

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:17.330
You're right, aren't you?
We're the only ones who can go, aren't we?

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.120
Sir...

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:24.290
Here. It's the family contact information
for the staff we lost at Tsukimijima.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.700
Thank you.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:27.790
Yes, that's right.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:31.160
I would like to stock up on
at least two weeks worth

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:33.540
of consumable parts up to Level C.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:38.290
Even so, we're barely able
to maintain our current shift.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.700
Please do something about that.

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:42.410
Thank you for adjusting the line. Bye!

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:44.580
You look busy.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:47.500
I guess. We're totally short on staff.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.290
And Yukiho isn't coming in.
Where on Earth did she go?

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:50.950
Huh?

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.830
But Suzushiro said she saw Yukiho in front
of the maintenance room just a minute ago.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:55.580
What?!
But Suzushiro said she saw Yukiho in front
of the maintenance room just a minute ago.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:57.250
When was that?!

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.080
Wh-when was what?

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:10.700
What happened?! Is it a blackout?

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:13.370
Someone go check the breaker!

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:18.080
The mainframe has been shut down!
We're losing the backup.

00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:19.700
The breaker is out.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:22.080
The central system plus all other systems
have been turned off.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:25.620
All of the systems? That's preposterous!

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:26.160
The various locations are
falling into disarray.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:27.120
Open up!
The various locations are
falling into disarray.

00:13:29.830 --> 00:13:33.250
The communications system and data-link
devices have ceased functioning!

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.370
The base has been completely isolated.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.330
The reserve system is
not responding either!

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:39.540
I can't believe it's happened
now of all times...

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:45.370
Imber and Nebula have entered
launch sequences.

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.370
They've what?! That can't be possible!

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:49.910
Who would do that?!

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.370
So that's the deal.

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:59.950
Yukiho, doesn't it look like
we really overturned the base?

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:03.120
The confusion is temporary
and will calm down momentarily.

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:04.450
But...

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:08.660
Quit dilly-dallying, Idiot Ribbon!

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:10.790
Let's hurry, Haruka.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:19.450
Huh? Imber?

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.790
He must be hesitant since
I'm in here with you.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:25.830
Oh, you think?

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:45.870
Prometheus 1, Imber: Deploy!

00:14:47.330 --> 00:14:50.500
Prometheus 2, Nebula: Deploy!

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:53.120
Stop their launch!

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:54.370
I won't make it in time!

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.540
Oh, my! Aren't those iDOLs?

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:13.500
Mama, it's Santa!

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:21.790
Now they've really done it. Those girls...

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:27.910
Sir?

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:31.500
I am going to leave things here to you.

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.580
I understand.

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:47.540
This is the point they designated.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:51.580
And a thick jungle surrounds
both sides of this river's banks.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.790
So they can't find us if we hug the river.

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.790
I think it would be hard for them to find us.

00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:59.620
Think it'll be that easy?

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:02.830
That's why we should split up.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:06.080
One of you could serve as the decoy
and approach from head on

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:07.870
while the other goes around back...

00:16:07.870 --> 00:16:10.200
...and looks for a chance to rescue Ami.

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:11.620
I guess that's the only choice.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:15.120
Nubilum's signal is coming
from our target location.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:18.290
Affiliation:

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:22.250
In that case, I'll be the decoy so Imber can-

00:16:22.250 --> 00:16:23.660
Wait, Iori.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.790
I'll be the decoy.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:28.290
What?! But...

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:29.700
Please!

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:36.450
Fine. I'll leave that to you.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:41.250
In exchange, make sure
to keep your guard up!

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:45.120
Uh-huh!

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:49.620
I want to speak with that lady once more...

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:09.370
She's here.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:16.120
Haruka...

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:23.580
Ami!

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:49.540
Isn't that... No way! It's an iDOL!

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:51.830
Long time no see, Minase.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:54.660
I see you've improved a bit.

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:57.410
Makoto?! What are you doing...?

00:17:58.330 --> 00:18:03.330
Allow me to introduce him.
This is my new partner, Hiems.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:29.700
I haven't seen you since Iceland.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:35.250
Chihaya, you love Imber, don't you?

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:39.660
That's what I thought when
I saw Imber's perception of you.

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:43.290
I thought you two must
have been really close.

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:45.700
That's right.

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:48.700
So please, don't do this!

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:56.660
I thought hard. Why would
Imber reject you, Chihaya?

00:18:57.290 --> 00:19:00.540
Why didn't he leave Mondenkind with you?

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:05.450
Imber doesn't want to hurt anybody.

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:09.160
He didn't want to become
a tool used to hurt others.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:11.120
That's why!

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:15.410
You may be right.

00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:18.200
Chihaya?

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:21.200
Ami!

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:26.120
I get how your mind works.

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.040
You're kind, straightforward, pure...

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:31.790
...and so arrogant that
it makes me want to puke!

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:37.580
I'm amazed you have the nerve to do
something like speak on Imber's behalf!

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:44.000
I will teach you who Imber truly belongs to.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:49.950
Yukiho...?

00:20:24.870 --> 00:20:28.040
What... is going on?

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:41.160
Makoto! Damn it! Damn it! DAMN IT!

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:43.790
Nebula, move!

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:48.750
Idiot Ribbon... Haruka is waiting for us.

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:53.450
Please, Nebula.

00:20:55.660 --> 00:20:58.370
Nebula...

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:08.750
Yukiho? Hey!

00:21:38.160 --> 00:21:40.370
Yukiho...?

00:21:56.410 --> 00:22:05.370
Toki o wataru seija no you ni

00:22:05.370 --> 00:22:14.330
Donna kodoku ni naite ita no?

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:23.200
Haruka tooi hoshi o tsunagi

00:22:23.200 --> 00:22:31.750
Ne, omoi o egaku wa, sora o miagete

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:43.200
Dear boy, itsumo kokoro ni anata o sagaseba

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:52.160
Ah, dakishimeru hodo ni tsuyoi hikari o hanatsu no

00:22:52.160 --> 00:23:01.120
Mabataku kidou ga futari no mejirushi

00:23:01.120 --> 00:23:12.700
Ima doko de mite ite mo truth kanjitete

00:23:26.080 --> 00:23:41.080
Preview:
Goodbye

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:29.120
Sir, doesn't this make you kinda nervous?

00:23:29.120 --> 00:23:33.000
Well, it is rather rare for me
to speak with another man...

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:35.160
Uh, what should we talk about?

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:38.450
Rather than speak with words,
men should speak with...

00:23:38.450 --> 00:23:40.660
Huh? Sir? Sir?!
